<task id="148" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C10 part 2 (transitions + backfill) — re-own EXISTING children when a record becomes secure (provisioning) and when it stops being secure (unsecure), for projects, matters and work assignments, plus a one-time backfill of every existing secure record's children: one engine, idempotent, resumable, reported, manual live gate</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C10 half 2, owner round 2 item 6 "backfill and transitions")</phase>
    <gate>after 144 (named team, generalized provisioning/unsecure, root migration applied in dev), 145 (child privileges), 146 (owner rule for children) and 149 (sharee mirror + reconcile) are merged.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Irreversible-in-effect live ownership changes on the secure-isolation boundary; modifies the provisioning and unsecure endpoints (tags bff-api, auth, security); adds a scheduled job.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Ordering-sensitive state transitions on a security boundary (a wrong order locks users out or leaves children exposed) plus a bulk live data change whose mistakes are silent.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs and UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs (also edited by 133, 139, 143, 144, 149 and the sprk_issecure-lock task 150) and registers its job in Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs (ExternalAccess exclusive zone — also edited by amended task 056); adds the reconciliation job that task 147 schedules. Serialize with each; whichever runs second rebases.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>144, 145, 146, 149</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, job, migration, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 27 C10 research gap 4 ("No backfill at provision or unsecure time"); owner round 2 item 6.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Task 146 makes NEW children of a secure record secure. Children that already exist when a record becomes secure — and children of records that are already secure today — are still owned in ordinary business units. Build ONE server-side engine that brings every existing child of a root into the state task 146 would have given it (owner + mirrored shares), call it when a root is provisioned secure and when it is unsecured, and run it once over every existing secure record.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer on the Dataverse write path and the secure-isolation boundary. Expert in Dataverse assign semantics, POA shares, and ADR-036 scheduled jobs. Fail closed; verify every write by read-back.</role>

  <goal>A `SecureChildReconciler` engine that, for one root, finds every child and grandchild (per live metadata and the FR-26 taxonomy), assigns each to the owner the task-146 rule gives it, and applies task 149's reconcile(root) — is called by provisioning (all three root types) after the root is isolated and shared, and by unsecure before the flag is cleared; a report-only-by-default sweep job runs it over every `sprk_issecure = true` root; every run is idempotent, resumable, and produces a per-root, per-table report; dev is backfilled and verified by hand.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>TRANSITION 1 — BECOMING SECURE. `Api/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs` re-owns only the root row (Step 5 `:474-508` → `AssignOwnerToSecureTeamAsync` `:597-616`), then shares it to the creator and colleagues (Step 5.5 `:510-521`), then creates and records the container (`:523-560`). Task 144 generalizes this to sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment and switches the owner to the named team. Nothing touches the root's EXISTING children: a project flagged secure after it already has documents, events, to-dos and communications leaves all of them in ordinary BUs.

TRANSITION 2 — STOPPING BEING SECURE. `Api/ExternalAccess/UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs` (sequence `:17-22`): reads the root (`:103-148`), resolves the new owner (`:150-166`), assigns the root to that user and verifies (`:168-226`), revokes every POA share on the root (`:227`, revoke `:373`), clears `sprk_issecure` last (`:231-262`). Its remarks explain the ordering: ownership moves BEFORE shares are revoked so the record is never reachable by nobody, and the flag clears last so the label never lies (`:28-43`). After task 146, the root's children are owned by the memberless Secure team and carry mirrored shares (task 149); unsecure leaves them there — orphaned, reachable by nobody once the root's shares are gone. Task 144 generalizes unsecure to matters and work assignments.

TRANSITION 3 — THE RECORDS THAT ARE ALREADY SECURE. Task 144's migration moves existing secure ROOTS to the named team; their children were never touched by anything. Dev today: 1 secure project, 0 documents linked to any secure root (session27 live facts) — the backfill must still be proven on seeded probe children, because production-shaped environments will not be empty.

WHAT "EVERY CHILD" MEANS. design.md §5.1d (`design.md:552-603`) enumerated 18 entities / 19 lookups on sprk_project from live metadata; matter and work assignment have their own sets (task 146 step 2 records all three). Children link three ways: (a) direct root lookups (`sprk_document`: `sprk_project`, `sprk_relatedproject`, `sprk_matter`, `sprk_workassignment`; `sprk_invoice`: `sprk_matter`, `sprk_project`); (b) FR-26 `sprk_regarding{core}` stamps on todo/event/communication/analysis (`Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:74-100`); (c) GRANDCHILDREN reached only through a child — `sprk_document` and `sprk_invoice` carry NO stamp columns (`notes/phase3-backfill-runbook.md` §1b), so a to-do regarding a document on a secure project has no stamp pointing at the project and is found only by walking document → to-do. Rows owned per-user by design (task 146's census waivers) and ROOT records with their own `sprk_issecure` (e.g. a work assignment under a project) are excluded as task 146 classifies them.

PRECEDENTS TO REUSE, NOT COPY. `scripts/Backfill-CoreAncestorStamps.ps1` (task 053 — dry-run default, idempotent, metadata-discovered columns) and word-add-in-r1's `scripts/Backfill-RecordOwnership.ps1` (write-ahead reversal manifest, read-back per assign, `-MaxWritesPerRun` sample cap — note 080 §6.9) show the operational shape. But the RULE must be the BFF's: the write-path architecture's key property is that inline (L1), fix-up (L3) and reconciliation (L4) call the SAME invariant owner classes (`DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md:81`). ADR-036 job precedents in this BFF: `Services/ExternalAccess/ExternalAccessReconciliationJob.cs:94` (registered disabled, writes report-only by default) and `Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipReconciliationJob.cs:146`.</background>
