  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a root with existing children (direct-lookup, stamped, and a grandchild reached only through a document), provisioning it secure (project, matter, work assignment) leaves every child owned by the named Secure team (read-back) with shares equal to the root's (task 149 rule), and the response reports per-table counts.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a secure root with secure-team-owned children, unsecure re-owns every child to the owner task 146's rule gives a non-secure parent, removes the mirrored child shares, then revokes the root's shares and clears the flag — in that order (asserted by call-order in the test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a child pass that cannot complete returns a stable reason code and a message with re-owned/remaining counts (never a bare 500); unsecure in that state leaves `sprk_issecure = true`; a second invocation completes the pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: unfiled documents, per-user rows, children of other roots, and child roots carrying their own `sprk_issecure` are never re-owned (fixtures include each as a decoy).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (never over-share): at no step of provisioning, unsecure or the sweep does a principal not shared on the root gain access to any child (asserted over the recorded call sequence in the transition tests, including an interrupted pass); an interrupted provisioning pass leaves children under-shared or still in their old owner, never readable by a new principal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Idempotence: a second reconcile or sweep run over the same state changes nothing and reports zero changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The sweep job is registered disabled and report-only by default; in report-only mode it writes nothing and reports every change it would make; with writes enabled it applies them with read-back and records previous owners.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AUTHORIZATION: provisioning and unsecure keep their existing delegation gate (Write on the SAME root, as the caller); a caller without it gets 403 and no child is touched.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev): the step-6 sequence is recorded — provision and unsecure transitions on seeded children for all three root types (owner read-back, share mirror, a non-sharee existing non-admin test user denied), the report-only sweep plan, the applied sweep over dev's existing secure roots, and a second sweep with zero changes; probes deleted and the deletion recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The guide contains the operator runbook (dry run, apply, verify); the write-path I-2 row states the L1 and L4 owners.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF unit/integration/ArchTests green; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the two transitions, the failure/resume, the exclusion decoys, idempotence and the job's two modes named above. Anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C10 half 2 (session26 note §C10 half 2; session27 note C10 research gap 4 and "Secure matters and work assignments are never re-owned"). Depends on 144 (named team, generalized endpoints, root migration), 145 (privileges), 146 (owner rule), 149 (share mirror). Task 147 turns this task's job into the scheduled L4 safety net for client-created children. Related: task 133 / C11 (creator-share failure / resumability on the same endpoint), task 150 (sprk_issecure lock — makes these two endpoints the only transitions).</notes>

