    <outcome date="2026-10-04" branch="task/uac-r2-148" base="e94a8bc2d (task/uac-r2-149-r4 + task/uac-r2-133-c1-r3.-r2 + work/unified-access-control-r2 734d05f26)">
      <summary>Code complete, NOT deployed; full record in notes/task-148-secure-child-backfill.md. ONE engine, Services/Access/SecureChildReconciler.cs, brings every EXISTING child of a root (descendants through task 149's lineage map, any owner, shallowest first, plus the SharePoint rows the root's own Assign cascades to) into the state task 146's rule gives it: the owner IRecordOwnershipResolver answers for the row's own parents (a row is moved ONLY across the isolation boundary; each assign its own update, read back, previous owner logged first), then the root's sharees via SecureChildShareSynchronizer.SyncRootAsync (into isolation) or the mirrored shares removed after the re-own (out). Triggers: provisioning Step 8 (after isolated + shared + container; task 149's former Step 8 folded in; incomplete -&gt; 500 sdap.provision.children_incomplete; a repeat call on the provisioned record completes it -&gt; 200 childrenOnly, else 409 as before); unsecure Step 2.5 (cascade rows read before the move, sdap.unsecure.cascade_children_unreadable) + Step 3.5 (after the root's move, BEFORE its shares are revoked and its flag cleared; incomplete -&gt; 500 sdap.unsecure.children_incomplete, the flag and the root's shares stay; on an already-unsecure record the call completes children a pre-148 unsecure left isolated; the SharePoint location/document rows take the 146 rule's owner -- owner round 13 item 1); NEW SecureChildReconciliationJob over every sprk_issecure root, ordered, capped, per-instance cursor, registered DISABLED and REPORT-ONLY (SecureChild:Reconciliation:WritesEnabled). One-time backfill = scripts/Invoke-SecureChildBackfill.ps1 (dry run default / -Apply / -Verify; only triggers the job and reads its reports). Provisioning order shipped is re-own -&gt; mirror (the constraint's fallback order; 149 mirrors only Secure-team-owned rows and shares may go ONLY through 149 -- transient under-share recorded, never an over-share). The resolver gains ONE named input, RecordOwnershipContext.UnsecuringRoot, so the root mid-unsecure (flag still set, cleared last) is not read as a failed provisioning; every other parent keeps every rule. No escalation trigger fired (dev census: one secure project, zero children).</summary>
